-- The tier owns AUTHORING: turning a trajectory into a completion list,
-- a monthly ledger into a schedule, and a free parameter into a calibrated
-- and REPORTED decision, plus what a validator can and cannot catch and the
-- security properties of a deck that arrived from outside. The Associate tier
-- owns reading the deck and the Professional tier owns the reconciliation and
-- the fluid and rock provenance; this tier assumes both and grades neither.
--
-- MODULE m05 'Reading Results' GRADES NOTHING, deliberately, and says so in
-- its own first lesson. @petrolord/engines emits decks and does geometry; it
-- has no flow solver, so this course has no simulated result to check an
-- answer against. Results literacy is taught because a deck writer who cannot
-- read a results file is writing blind, and grading it would mean grading
-- against numbers nobody has checked. Same treatment RC4 gave to enhanced
-- recovery screening.
--
-- Numeric provenance: every literal is engine-derived. rc5_numsweep.mjs runs
-- the vendored engines through the course's own teaching lab
-- (src/components/course/panels/sim/simLab.js) and sweeps the wave's lessons
-- and banks: 0 unresolved over lessons, 0 over banks. rc5_leakage.mjs sweeps
-- both for a lower tier printing a higher tier's graded value: 0 leaks.
-- The live capstone answer key (applied in 20260828_rc5_sim_course.sql):
--   deviated_connection_count 11 (tol 0),
