-- ONE FIELD WAS REPLACED BEFORE SEEDING. The tier originally graded the
-- column-tapered volumetric convention, which Professional m02 owns outright
-- and teaches at full precision. It was replaced by
-- `calibration_regional_mean_m`, the tuned kriging parameter, which no lower
-- tier prints and which can only be obtained by running the bisection.
--
-- THE TIER'S CENTRAL FACT: a calibration is not a validation. One free
-- parameter was tuned against one trusted number, so the model cannot fail
-- the comparison, only be adjusted until it agrees. Ekene has no spare well,
-- so the static model is calibrated and carries NO independent structural
-- check, and saying that is the most useful line in the report.
-- THE TIER'S SHARPEST LESSON, and the one that cost the most to get right:
-- the seven broken specifications must each trip exactly ONE rule. The first
-- attempt replaced the whole wells list, which left a 36-period history naming
-- five absent wells and produced 180 errors on a case advertised as isolated.
-- A cascading negative test still fails, so the suite still passes, and six of
-- the seven rules are never exercised on their own. The generator now asserts
-- that no case raises more than two errors (engines PR #65), which is why the
-- graded count of 7 CASES is meaningful and the 8 MESSAGES is not.
--
-- Bank QA before seeding (recorded in migrations/docs/rc5-sim-pentest.md):
-- length-rank gate green per served pool (rank 0 share 27 pct over the tier,
-- rank 3 share 27 pct, no pool above 29 pct), within-pool Jaccard < 0.50,
-- balanced non-cyclic keys, no em or en dashes, no positional references, and
-- no duplicate prompt anywhere in the wave.
-- ============================================================================

